🚀 Steps to Deploy from GitLab to Ge using Automated Pipeline
1. Prepare the Environment

Before pipeline setup, ensure the following:

✅ Access to Gen servers or environment (SSH, VPN, or cloud endpoint)

✅ Deployment credentials (SSH key, service account, or API token)

✅ GitLab Runner installed and registered (can be shell, SSH, or Kubernetes executor)

✅ Deployment target (e.g., EC2 instance, on-prem VM, or Kubernetes cluster in Gen)

4. Secure Access to Gen

If the target is on-prem in Gen, ensure:

GitLab Runner’s IP is whitelisted in the firewall.

SSH key added to /home/<user>/.ssh/authorized_keys on the target host.


5. Monitor & Verify Deployment

After pipeline runs:

Check GitLab CI/CD Job Logs for success confirmation.

Validate the application is reachable at its Gen endpoint.

Optionally, use a post-deploy script to:

Run health checks

Send Slack/email notifications

Rollback if failed
If the target is AWS Europe (Gen region) or similar, configure via IAM role or API credentials instead of SSH.
